---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Advertising Disclosure | FindPIAttorney.com"
  description="Understand how FindPIAttorney.com generates revenue, how paid listings work, and how we maintain editorial independence in our attorney directory."
  canonical="https://www.findpiattorney.com/advertising-disclosure"
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="bg-brand-900 text-white py-14">
      <div class="page-container text-center">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white/10 text-white text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full mb-4 border border-white/20">
          Legal Document
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Advertising Disclosure</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-brand-200 max-w-xl mx-auto text-sm">
          We believe in complete transparency. Here is exactly how our directory works, how we generate revenue, and what that means for you.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-brand-300">Last Updated: August 17, 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Effective: August 17, 2026</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-container section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">

        <!-- Quick Summary -->
        <div class="bg-brand-50 border border-brand-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-brand-900 mb-3 uppercase tracking-wide">At a Glance</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-brand-800">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 mt-0.5">✓</span> Most attorney listings are free and sourced from public bar records.</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 mt-0.5">✓</span> Paid or sponsored placements are clearly labeled "Sponsored."</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 mt-0.5">✓</span> Paying for placement does not imply endorsement or higher quality.</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 mt-0.5">✓</span> We always recommend verifying credentials independently.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-10 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">

          <!-- Section 1 -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-500 pl-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">1. Who We Are</h2>
            <p>
              FindPIAttorney.com is an independent online directory listing personal injury attorneys licensed in Florida, New Jersey, and Texas. We are not a law firm, attorney referral service, or legal counsel. We compile our listings from publicly available state bar records.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3">
              This Advertising Disclosure is provided in accordance with the Federal Trade Commission (FTC) guidelines on endorsements and testimonials (16 C.F.R. Part 255), as well as applicable state bar rules regarding attorney advertising and referral services.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 2 -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-500 pl-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">2. How Our Directory Is Populated</h2>
            <p>The vast majority of attorney profiles on this Site are compiled from <strong>publicly available records</strong> maintained by:</p>
            <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside text-sm">
              <li>The Florida Bar (floridabar.org)</li>
              <li>The New Jersey State Bar Association and related licensing authorities</li>
              <li>The State Bar of Texas (texasbar.com)</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-3">
              These profiles include name, bar number, firm, location, and licensure status. <strong>Attorneys do not pay to be included in our standard directory listings.</strong> Inclusion in the directory does not indicate that an attorney has consented to or is aware of their listing.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 3 -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-500 pl-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">3. Paid & Sponsored Placements</h2>
            <p>
              FindPIAttorney.com may offer attorneys and law firms the opportunity to purchase enhanced visibility on our platform. Any such paid placement will be <strong>prominently and clearly identified</strong> using one or more of the following labels:
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
              <div class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-200 rounded-xl p-3 text-center">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-yellow-800 uppercase tracking-wide">Sponsored</span>
                <p class="text-xs text-yellow-700 mt-1">Paid placement</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-200 rounded-xl p-3 text-center">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-yellow-800 uppercase tracking-wide">Featured</span>
                <p class="text-xs text-yellow-700 mt-1">Promoted listing</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-200 rounded-xl p-3 text-center">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-yellow-800 uppercase tracking-wide">Advertisement</span>
                <p class="text-xs text-yellow-700 mt-1">Paid content</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-4">
              Paid placements may appear at the top of search results, city pages, or state pages. However, <strong>payment does not influence our editorial content, factual reporting, or the criteria by which any attorney is evaluated or described.</strong>
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 4 -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-500 pl-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">4. No Endorsement</h2>
            <p>
              <strong>Inclusion in this directory - whether free or paid - does not constitute an endorsement, recommendation, certification, or guarantee of quality by FindPIAttorney.com.</strong>
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3">
              We do not evaluate attorneys' competence, ethics, disciplinary records, case outcomes, client satisfaction ratings, or fitness for any specific legal matter. Any attorney you contact through this directory should be independently evaluated by you prior to retention.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 5 -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-500 pl-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">5. Affiliate & Referral Relationships</h2>
            <p>
              From time to time, FindPIAttorney.com may display links, banners, or content from third-party services or partners. If we have a material financial relationship with such a third party (e.g., we earn a commission or fee if you click a link or complete an action), this will be disclosed clearly at the point of that content.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3">
              We do not receive any commission, fee, or referral payment from attorneys solely because a user contacts or retains them through this directory. Our standard listings are not pay-per-lead.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 6 -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-500 pl-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">6. Editorial Independence</h2>
            <p>
              All informational articles, guides, and FAQs published on FindPIAttorney.com are written independently for educational purposes. They are not written on behalf of, sponsored by, or influenced by any attorney or law firm. Our editorial content is not legal advice and is not intended to serve as a substitute for professional legal counsel.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 7 -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-500 pl-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">7. FTC Compliance</h2>
            <p>
              This disclosure is provided in compliance with the Federal Trade Commission's guidelines requiring clear and conspicuous disclosure of material connections between advertisers and publishers. We are committed to honest and transparent advertising practices.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3">
              If you believe any content on this Site fails to meet this standard, please contact us immediately at <a href="mailto:info@findpiattorney.com" class="text-brand-700 underline font-medium">info@findpiattorney.com</a>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 8 -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-500 pl-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">8. State Bar Rule Compliance</h2>
            <p>
              Attorney advertising in Florida, New Jersey, and Texas is governed by specific rules of professional conduct. Attorneys who purchase enhanced listings on FindPIAttorney.com are solely responsible for ensuring that their content, communications, and advertising practices comply with all applicable rules of their state bar, including but not limited to:
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside text-sm">
              <li>Florida Rules of Professional Conduct, Rule 4-7 (Lawyer Advertising)</li>
              <li>New Jersey Rules of Professional Conduct, Rule 7.1–7.5 (Information About Legal Services)</li>
              <li>Texas Disciplinary Rules of Professional Conduct, Part VII (Information About Legal Services)</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-3">FindPIAttorney.com is not an attorney referral service as defined under Florida Bar Rule 4-7.22 or any analogous New Jersey or Texas regulation.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 9 -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-500 pl-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">9. Your Responsibility</h2>
            <p>
              Before retaining any attorney found through this directory, we strongly encourage you to:
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm">
              <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-600 font-bold">→</span> Verify the attorney's current license status on your state bar's official website</li>
              <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-600 font-bold">→</span> Check for any disciplinary history or public sanctions</li>
              <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-600 font-bold">→</span> Confirm the attorney's experience with your specific type of case</li>
              <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-600 font-bold">→</span> Understand all fee arrangements in writing before signing any agreement</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 10 -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-500 pl-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">10. Contact Us</h2>
            <p>
              For questions about advertising opportunities, sponsored listings, or this disclosure, please contact us:
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 text-sm space-y-2">
              <p><strong>FindPIAttorney.com</strong></p>
              <p>Email: <a href="mailto:info@findpiattorney.com" class="text-brand-700 underline font-medium">info@findpiattorney.com</a></p>
              <p>Response time: Within 30 business days</p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
